# Neo Prism parameters (docs/specs/neo-prism.md). The order changes only with a version (machines.md §3.2): songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoPrism
namespace NeoBuzz.Prism
class NeoPrismMachine
tracks 1
summary Spectral effect on a short-time spectrum (FFT 1024 to 8192, 4x overlap) with five sections that can all run, in this order: Spectral pitch (a semitone and cents shift, phase-locked so a chord stays clear, with Formant keep), Scramble (swaps bins within bands, seeded, at a rate or in sync), Freeze (holds the spectrum, from a switch, a note or the song), Blur (smooths the spectrum over up to 4 s and across frequency) and Spectral delay (a delay that tilts from low to high frequencies, with feedback and damping). Mix and Amount; the reported latency is one frame. Use it for frozen chords, washed pads, bin-shuffle glitches, shimmer, formant-kept pitch shifts and rising spectral echoes.

group Spectral pitch
PitchOn         "Pitch"              0 1 0       switch                                       | The spectral pitch shift: on or off
    how Turns the spectral pitch shift on or off.
    sound On, every partial in the sound moves by the same number of semitones.
Semi            "Semitones"          0 48 24     int -24 st signed                            | Shift in semitones, -24 to +24
    how Sets the shift in whole semitones.
    sound Seven up is a fifth above, twelve up an octave, twelve down an octave below.
Cents           "Cents"              0 200 100   int -100 cents signed                        | Fine shift in cents, added to the semitones
    how Adds a fine shift in cents (a hundredth of a semitone) to the semitones.
    sound A few cents make a slow chorus-like beat against the dry sound; use it with Mix.
FormantKeep     "Formant keep"       0 1 0       switch                                       | Keeps the spectral envelope (the formants) where it was while the partials move
    how Moves the partials but keeps the broad spectral envelope in place.
    sound A voice shifted up still sounds like the same person instead of a chipmunk.
group Scramble
ScrOn           "Scramble"           0 1 0       switch                                       | The bin scramble: on or off
    how Turns the bin scramble on or off.
    sound On, the bins inside each band are shuffled between themselves.
ScrAmount       "Scramble amount"    0 1000 500  pct                                          | The share of the bins that are swapped
    how Sets the share of the bins in each band that are moved.
    sound Low values blur the detail a little, high values turn the sound into a glitchy cloud.
ScrWidth        "Band width"         2 64 8      int 0                                        | Bins that are shuffled together (a band)
    how Sets how many neighbouring bins are shuffled between themselves.
    sound Narrow bands keep the tone and add grit, wide ones scatter the pitch.
ScrSync         "Scramble sync"      0 6 0       enum Free 1/16 1/8 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars      | How often the shuffle changes: Free (the Rate in Hz) or a length in the song
    how Chooses whether a new shuffle comes at a free rate or on the beat grid of the song.
    sound Synced shuffles change in time with the music, free ones drift.
ScrRate         "Scramble rate"      0 1000 565  exp 0.1 20 Hz 2                              | New shuffles per second, when the sync is Free
    how Sets how many new shuffles come each second.
    sound Slow rates give a stable scatter, fast rates a fizzing texture.
ScrSeed         "Scramble seed"      0 99 1      int 0                                        | The seed of the shuffles: the same seed always gives the same sequence
    how Picks which sequence of shuffles is used.
    sound Different seeds give different glitch textures; the same seed repeats exactly.
group Freeze
FreezeOn        "Freeze"             0 1 0       switch                                       | Holds the current spectrum (when the trigger is Switch)
    how Holds the spectrum as it is now, each partial running on at its own frequency.
    sound The sound turns into a steady, endless chord made from what was playing.
FreezeTrig      "Freeze trigger"     0 2 0       enum Switch Note Synced                      | What freezes: the Freeze switch, a note, or the song
    how Chooses whether the switch, a held note or the beat grid freezes the sound.
    sound Note freezes for as long as a key is down, Synced catches the sound at the start of every period.
FreezeEvery     "Freeze every"       0 4 2       enum 1_beat 2_beats 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars      | Synced: how often a new freeze is caught
    how Sets how often a synced freeze catches the sound.
    sound Short periods make a stepping chord, long ones hold a pad for bars.
FreezeLen       "Freeze length"      0 4 3       enum 1/16 1/8 1/4 1/2 1_bar                  | Synced: how long each freeze is held
    how Sets how long each synced freeze is held.
    sound Short holds clip the frozen sound off between catches.
Hold            "Hold blend"         0 1000 1000 pct                                          | How much of the output is frozen (100 %) and how much live; fades over at least 20 ms
    how Blends the live and the frozen spectrum; the change takes at least 20 ms.
    sound Half and half lets new notes ring over the held chord.
group Blur
BlurOn          "Blur"               0 1 0       switch                                       | The spectral blur: on or off
    how Turns the blur on or off.
    sound On, the sound is smeared in time and in frequency.
BlurTime        "Blur time"          0 1000 354  pow 0 4000 2 ms 0                            | Smooths each bin's level over this time
    how Sets how slowly each frequency's level follows the sound.
    sound Long times wash notes into a pad that outlasts them.
Smear           "Smear"              0 24 0      int 0                                        | Smooths the level across this many bins either side
    how Spreads each frequency's level over its neighbours.
    sound Smear softens the tone into a wash without changing its pitch.
group Spectral delay
DelayOn         "Delay"              0 1 0       switch                                       | The spectral delay: on or off
    how Turns the spectral delay on or off.
    sound On, low and high frequencies come back at different times.
DelLow          "Low time"           0 1000 224  pow 0 2000 2 ms 0                            | Delay of the lowest frequencies
    how Sets the delay time at the bottom of the spectrum.
    sound Short low times with long high times make the highs trail behind.
DelHigh         "High time"          0 1000 447  pow 0 2000 2 ms 0                            | Delay of the highest frequencies
    how Sets the delay time at the top of the spectrum.
    sound Long high times make a rising or falling spectral echo.
DelSync         "Delay sync"         0 4 0       enum Free 1/16 1/8 1/4 1/2                   | Free: the times as set; otherwise each time is rounded to a multiple of this note at the song's tempo
    how Rounds both delay times to a multiple of a note length of the song.
    sound Synced delays echo in time with the music.
DelFeedback     "Feedback"           0 1000 404  lin 0 99 % 0                                 | Share of the delayed spectrum fed back in (kept below 100 %)
    how Feeds the delayed sound back into the delay.
    sound More feedback gives more repeats; it is always kept below 100 % so it dies away.
DelDamping      "Damping"            0 1000 300  pct                                          | Extra loss of high frequencies at every repeat
    how Makes each repeat darker than the one before.
    sound High damping turns the repeats into a dark, fading wash.
group Output
FftSize         "FFT size"           0 3 2       enum 1024 2048 4096 8192                     | Frame size: larger is smoother for tones and pads, smaller is tighter for beats; also the latency (size minus 1)
    how Sets the size of the analysis frame, which is also the latency.
    sound Small frames keep drums sharp, large ones keep chords and pads clean.
Mix             "Mix"                0 1000 1000 pct                                          | Dry/wet (the dry signal is delayed by the latency)
    how Blends the processed sound with the dry input.
    sound Lower values keep the original and lay the effect on top.
Amount          "Amount"             0 1000 500  lin 0 200 % 0                                | Effect strength: 100 % = the settings as they stand, 0 = clean (bit for bit the input), 200 % = exaggerated
    how Scales the shift, the scramble, the blur, the delay times and the feedback together.
    sound Turn it down to fade the effect out, up to push it harder; at 0 the sound is clean.
